// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ending E6 "Final image: the dark sea" (C, 1.5 min). act3_ending.md §2 E6; N-01, N-14,
// N-17, N-19. Haluna's dock at night; ONE LOCKED SHOT, front three-quarter on her face (camera on the planks ~4 m
// shoreward, eye height 1.5 m, 50 mm, looking out to sea). Asha at the dock's end, alive, a SECOND REACH-BAND on her
// forearm. The sea is COMPLETELY DARK (sea_glow 0.0 from the cut), the stars reflected in it. She turns ~50° toward
// Haluna, draws breath for the tune, LETS IT GO UNSUNG, AND SMILES. Rhen's older voice-over: one or two lines, gentle,
// still a little funny, ≤ 25 words each. No cut, no push. `ending_dock`: solo piano, the Hush's first phrase resolving.
title: ending_the_dark_sea
location: ch02/haluna
---
@letterbox on
@fade in 3.0
@camera E11
@music ending_dock fade=2.0
@wait 6.0
@anim asha turn_to haluna
@wait 3.0
@anim asha draw_breath
@wait 4.0
@anim asha smile
@wait 4.0
Narrator(rhen) [tender]: She never sang again. She says the stars do it better now. She's wrong, but I let her have it. #line:ending_sea_001 #vo
@wait 4.0
Narrator(rhen) [tender]: Everyone I told you about is gone. I remembered. #line:ending_sea_002 #vo #tn:"Answers the Prologue's 'Remember that, later.' Quiet, not a flourish."
@wait 6.0
@fade out 4.0
@letterbox off
===
